WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.200
-Our next guest
is an Emmy-nominated comedian

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.934
who you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.801
which is all-new this week,
with host Paul Rudd

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:11.234
and musical guest Charli XCX.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.901
Please welcome Bowen Yang!

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh!

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:18.133
That's what I'm talk--
Oh, come on, now!

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.734
Bowen!
-Hi!

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.501
-Thank you for coming on.
Last time you were here,

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:25.033
we were talking about
how you played the iceberg

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.767
that sank the Titanic.

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.901
And it was a giant hit,
and it was so funny.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.767
And since then, you got
nominated for an Emmy for that.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.834
-Thanks.
Thanks, everybody.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.634
-How did it go?
How was the Emmys?

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.601
Was it all
like you thought it would be?

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.367
-Yeah.
It was everything I dreamed of,

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.367
because it took place in a tent

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.534
on top of a parking garage
in Los Angeles.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.033
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.934
-And I feel like that's
the Emmy experience, baby.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.801
No, it was so fun.
I got to hug Jean Smart.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.200
I got to give her an award,
technically.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.968
And then, I got to, like,
eat little prosciutto things

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.400
next to Lorne Michaels
and joke with him all night,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.100
so it was lovely.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.634
-I like seeing you
and talking to you

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.133
about the things
that you experience.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.767
'Cause I know you got excited

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.601
that Taylor Swift
was on the show.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.033
Musical guest
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:20.501
a few weeks ago, and you're
a big Taylor swift fan.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.901
-Big Swiftie.
-I know you're a big Swiftie.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.968
And did you get to meet her,
and were you nervous?

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.067
And walk me through the process.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.234
-I got to meet her
at promos on Thursday.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.868
When you're shooting promos
for the episode,

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.267
you do that on Thursday.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.767
People at "SNL" threw me a bone,

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.801
said that,
"You can stand next to her."

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.334
It was a huge deal.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.767
I got to tell her that
in an improvised line in a promo

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.701
that her song "Treacherous"
is the sound of falling in love,

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.434
which I believe to be true.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.701
And then, I stood outside
of her dressing room

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.434
after the show on Saturday...
-Now we're talking.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.767
Now we're talking.
Yeah.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:58.667
-Yeah, okay.
This is the meat of it, okay?

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.501
I was not sure whether or not
to knock on her door.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.767
Because, it's a real, like...
You know, sometimes you don't --

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.567
Sometimes they say, like,
"Don't meet your heroes."

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.067
She's a hero.
And she was lovely all week.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.434
But I was like,
you know, after the show,

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.834
she's probably riding high.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.000
She doesn't want to talk to,
like, the riffraff like me.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.567
And so,
I finally knocked on her door.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.133
She couldn't have been nicer.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.300
And I said,
"I don't normally do this,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.501
but can we please
take a picture?"

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.200
And then, she was like,
"Of course!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.567
Can Sadie Sink,
the star and the muse

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.267
of my music video, be in it?"

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.868
I was like, "Of course!"
-I love Sadie Sink.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.801
-So we took this photo.
-I want to show the photo.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:32.767
Here's you,
Taylor, and Sadie Sink.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.834
Look at this.
Is that a perfect photo?

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.734
Now look at that.
[ Applause ]

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.767
-Pure bliss.
I'm blissed out.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:42.033
Then, there's more.
So, other people

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:44.367
in the dressing room were there,

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.400
and she was like,
"Who should take this?"

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.067
And then, Deadpool himself,
Ryan Reynolds was like,

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:52.467
"I'll do it."
That's him.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:55.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.267
The star of "Just Friends"
himself, yes.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:02.000
-How fun is that?
I want to --

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.634
This is the holiday show
coming up right now on "SNL."

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.200
Will you do anything
over the break?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.033
Are you gonna
get to see your family?

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.300
-Yeah. I'm just gonna
hang with my parents

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.200
and, like, teach my mom
how to use Netflix

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.601
for the eighth year in a row,
so I can't wait.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:18.400
-You posted some photos
of a hike.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.367
They're from --
Is it Denver?

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.367
Where are they from?
Colorado?

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.133
-Denver.
Suburban Denver.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.968
-They were going on a hike,
or hiking,

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.801
and you took photos
of your parents hiking.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.167
And fans of yours on Twitter
seemed a little confused

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.434
that these
are their hiking outfits.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.267
They look line they're going
to a dinner somewhere.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.534
[ Laughter ]
Pretty glamorous.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:38.133
-They're wearing, like,
steakhouse attire, basically.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.801
-Yeah, they are.
-They look --

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:43.000
They look, like, dressed up.
You know?

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.200
-Your dad's wearing loafers,
yeah.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.667
-Loafers.
My dad's wearing loafers

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.767
and a button-down
and, like, a sweater vest.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:53.534
My mom was wearing, like,
a Rhinestone/Swarovski crystal

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:56.400
sweatshirt that she bought
at Goodwill.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.701
And a lot of people
had a lot to say about

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:02.434
what they were wearing.
And I just had to be like,

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:05.567
"Y'all, this is
what immigrants do.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:07.501
They don't dress appropriately
for things,

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.734
and that's fine, and we should
let them do that."

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.400
Like, this is not actually
a steakhouse,

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.501
and there is no dress code
for this,

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.701
and I'm not gonna be
the person to tell them about

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.667
Dick's Sporting Goods or Ariano.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:22.167
-Why can't you be the person
that tells them that?

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:25.234
-I don't want to ruin
their innocence, you know?

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.501
I feel like the roles
have switched, and I don't want

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:30.100
to, like -- I want to, like,
keep them the way they are.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.033
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:35.734
I want to congratulate you
on your podcast, by the way.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.667
"Las Culturistas"?

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.033
Am I saying it correctly?
-Nailed it.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.834
-Thank you.
-Nailed.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.868
-You got named one of
the best comedy podcasts of 2021

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:45.701
by Vulture.
Congrats on that, buddy.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:50.868
Thank you so much.
Yeah, it's a real honor.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:53.634
-This weekend, Paul Rudd
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:56.234
-Paul Rudd, yeah.
-I mean he's the best.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.334
What can we expect?

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.834
Anything --
Can you give us any hints?

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:05.434
-I think you're gonna see
Mr. Rudd just be

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:08.167
Sexiest Man Aliving
all over the place.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.734
And I think that'll be great.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:15.033
I think it's his fifth time
hosting, so that's kind of cool.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:18.133
-Oh, maybe a Five Timers?
Maybe a five --

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:20.133
-Maybe a Five Timers moment.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.534
I don't know.
-All right.

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:22.701
-I can't say much more
than that.

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:23.734
-There you go.
I love you.

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:26.033
Bowen yang.
Thank you for the scoop.

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:27.968
Check out "Saturday Night Live"
this weekend

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:31.300
with host Paul Rudd,
musical guest Charli XCX.

